WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.345
Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun.

00:02.819 --> 00:06.769
It is also known as the "Red Planet", for its orange-red appearance.

00:07.246 --> 00:13.287
Mars is a desert-like rocky planet with a tenuous atmosphere that is primarily carbon dioxide.

00:13.794 --> 00:25.614
At the average surface level the atmospheric pressure is a few thousandths of Earth's, atmospheric temperature ranges from −153 to 20 °C, and cosmic radiation is high.

00:26.279 --> 00:39.714
Mars retains some water, in the ground as well as thinly in the atmosphere, forming cirrus clouds, fog, frost, larger polar regions of permafrost and ice caps, but no bodies of liquid surface water.
